{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfrwu3YbMigC7riHbmapk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The `fetcher` package is now async, and all 6 tests pass (`python -m pytest -q tests`).\n\n- **`fetcher/client.py`**:\n  - `get`, `get_many`, `close`, `async with` and the default transport (now using `asyncio.sleep`) are all async.\n  - `get_many` runs requests concurrently, limited by `max_concurrency` (default 5). Results keep input order, and per-URL errors come back as `FetchError` in the list.\n  - Retries use the same policy as before: `retries` attempts, exponential backoff, and only `TransientError` is retried.\n- **`fetcher/aggregate.py`**: `summarize` is async and returns the same shape.\n- **`fetcher/sync.py`** (new): `fetch_all(urls, transport=None)` runs `get_many` through `asyncio.run`.\n- **`tests/test_client.py`**: the three original tests are ported using plain `asyncio.run`. I added three more:\n  - retry exhaustion, and no retry on non-transient errors;\n  - the concurrency limit plus result order;\n  - the sync wrapper.\n\nI haven't committed anything."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2891,"cache_read_input_tokens":24954,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2891},"output_tokens":380,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"abaabbfa-663e-442a-8015-40a1807c9c8c","uuid":"2830875f-9276-4087-97eb-fa23eed10131","timestamp":"2026-10-09T16:04:31.371Z","request_id":"req_011Cfrwu3Gxxo4NccsWHBUZs"}
